  "Question": "A geometric sequence has \\(a_1=2\\) and \\(q=3\\). What is the sum of its first 4 terms?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "80",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(S_4=2\\times(81-1)/2=80\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Generate and add the four terms\n\nThere are only four terms, so we can add them directly. Multiplying each term by the common ratio \\(3\\) gives \\(2,6,18,54\\). Therefore the sum of the first four terms is\n\\[\n2+6+18+54=80.\n\\]",
